<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Nasir Bu Shentuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1524">1524</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-nasir">Muhammad ibn Nasir</a> Bu Shentuf was the last important emir of the Hintata, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masmuda">Masmuda</a> Berber dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in the early 16th century. Pressed between the Portuguese on the Atlantic coast and the rising Saadi sharifs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sous">Sous</a>, he was assassinated in 1524, and the Saadis entered Marrakesh around 1525 and made it their capital.</p></div>
